{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_exceeded_2.march","start_line":33,"start_col":2,"end_line":35,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileRead` (reached from `main`: main → slurp → File.read). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileRead` does not raise it.\nhelp: add a `Cap(IO.FileRead)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_fileread : Cap(IO.FileRead))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.","code":"cap_grant_exceeded","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
